# The live session's screen lock: it still engages, it just stops asking for a password.
#
# LIVE MEDIUM ONLY. Stage 40 installs this for the `installer` profile and nowhere else, next to
# 49-installer.rules and installer-autostart.desktop, and for the same reason those two exist:
# @LIVE_USER@'s password is printed in this medium's own documentation, so a prompt for it is
# theatre. Here it is worse than theatre — the polkit prompt at least stands in front of
# something the user asked for, while this one appears five minutes into an install they walked
# away from and reads, to anyone who does not know the account, as a machine that locked itself.
# The product image keeps a normal lock screen, and so does a machine installed from this medium:
# removeuser deletes @LIVE_USER@ and the account Calamares creates is an ordinary one, on a root
# that never carried this file.
#
# /etc/xdg, not a skel copy — same layer and same reasoning as /etc/xdg/baloofilerc. KConfig
# cascades $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS underneath ~/.config, so this is the image's default and System
# Settings -> Screen Locking still writes a user's own choice to ~/.config/kscreenlockerrc and
# wins over it.
#
# ONE KEY, and it is upstream's own rather than a PAM edit, because kscreenlocker already has an
# answer for exactly this. CONFIRMED against kscreenlocker 6.6.6, the version this image pins:
#
#   settings/kscreenlockersettings.kcfg names the file `kscreenlockerrc`, the group [Daemon] and
#   the key RequirePassword — "Sets whether the password is required to unlock the screen".
#
#   ksldapp.cpp reads it into m_requirePassword and acts on it in three places. lock() starts the
#   greeter with --nolock, which greeter/main.cpp documents as "Don't show any lock user
#   interface" — for an idle lock no password field is drawn at all, that path locking Delayed so
#   --immediateLock is absent. userActivity() calls unlock() on the first input event. And the
#   Lock Session global shortcut locks Delayed rather than Immediate.
#
#   The Wayland half matters here, because this image has no X11 session and X11Locker is what
#   emits userActivity() in kscreenlocker's own code. On Wayland the compositor does it instead:
#   kwin 6.6.6's src/input.cpp LockScreenFilter calls KSldApp::userActivity() on pointer motion,
#   buttons, axis and keys. So the unlock-on-activity path is live in the session we ship.
#
#   One caller still draws the UI: the D-Bus Lock() that Plasma's own Lock button and
#   `loginctl lock-session` go through, which interface.cpp always issues as Immediate. Even
#   there the first mouse move or keypress unlocks — the prompt is never answered, only seen.
#
# Autolock is deliberately left ON. Turning it off is a larger change with a different
# justification (a stick on a desk mid-install would never blank), and it is not what stands
# between the user and the installer. Add `Autolock=false` here if that changes.
[Daemon]
RequirePassword=false
